<!--
    swiftself read after a call, and the self of an imported Swift method
    (`option swiftcall on|off`).

    Issue: a function the metadata did not bind took swiftself (r13 / x20)
    only when its body read the register before its first call, so a closure
    that calls a function first read its context as an uninitialised local
    (`int8 v3; // r13`). A call to an imported Swift method such as
    `String.append(_:)` kept the C model, so the address of the string it
    appends to, passed in swiftself, was dropped.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 prototype recovery. `p4_calls/kuna_swiftinfer.rs
    (probe_reads)` walks past calls, which preserve the register; the
    `swiftcall` arm (`kuna-analysis analyzers/swift/kuna_swiftcall.rs (bind)`)
    binds the Swift model to the stub of every import whose symbol demangles
    to a method.

    The fixture `swift_self_elf` is a stripped swiftc 6.4.2 build of
    `swift_self_elf.swift` (recipe in the fixtures README): 0x2250 is the
    partial-apply forwarder of `makeReader`'s closure, 0x24b0 is `label`.
    Pass 1 (`option swiftcall off`) is the BUG, pass 2 (the default) the FIX.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/swift_self_elf</com>
  <com>option swiftmetadata on</com>
  <com>option swiftcall off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2250</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x24b0</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/swift_self_elf</com>
  <com>option swiftmetadata on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2250</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x24b0</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
